  "id": "COMPOUND:40805 - PROTEIN:4953",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Daphnetin-8-glucoside may interact with HEp-2 cells through a series of molecular pathways. The primary target of Daphnetin-8-glucoside appears to be an EDD domain protein from the DegV family, which is subsequently targeted by 2alpha-Hydroxytirotundin and 6(2H)-Benzofuranone, both of which also target HEp-2. This indicates a potential cascade of interactions where Daphnetin-8-glucoside may influence the activity of these proteins, ultimately affecting HEp-2 cells. The scores from the three paths are consistent, suggesting a reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role of Daphnetin-8-glucoside in modulating cellular processes within HEp-2, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise biological effects.",
